Problem Statement
Project Title
AI-Powered Discovery Engine for Understanding User Shopping Behavior in Quick Commerce: A Growth Case Study for Blinkit
Background
The quick-commerce industry in India has experienced rapid growth, with platforms such as Blinkit, Zepto, Instamart, and BigBasket competing to provide ultra-fast grocery and essentials delivery. While these platforms generate millions of user interactions across app stores, social media, online communities, and discussion forums, much of this feedback remains unstructured and difficult to analyze at scale.
For product managers, understanding why users purchase repeatedly, what drives category exploration, what frustrations they experience, and what unmet needs remain is essential for making data-driven product decisions. Manual analysis of thousands of reviews is time-consuming, inconsistent, and incapable of capturing emerging behavioral trends across multiple platforms.
This project aims to solve this problem by building an AI-powered discovery engine that automatically collects, cleans, aggregates, analyzes, validates, and visualizes user feedback from multiple public sources to generate actionable product insights.

Problem Statement
Design and develop an AI-powered Discovery Engine that automatically collects user-generated content related to Blinkit from multiple public sources and analyzes it to generate validated behavioral insights that can be used for product growth decisions in a Blinkit Product Management Case Study.
The system should gather large-scale user feedback from app stores, Reddit, community forums, social media discussions, product review websites, and quick-commerce discussions. It should then clean and deduplicate the data, identify recurring themes using AI, merge duplicate themes across different sources, validate the findings against raw data, and present the results through an interactive dashboard with supporting evidence and source citations.
The final solution should help product managers understand user behavior, recurring pain points, shopping habits, category exploration patterns, unmet needs, and opportunities for improving customer engagement and retention.

Objectives
The discovery engine should:
Collect large-scale user feedback from multiple online platforms.
Aggregate all collected data into a unified dataset.
Remove duplicate and low-quality records.
Identify recurring customer themes using AI/NLP.
Merge semantically similar themes appearing across multiple sources.
Rank themes by occurrence and source diversity.
Validate generated themes against the original dataset using keyword-based analysis.
Generate presentation-ready insights backed by supporting evidence.
Display all findings in an intuitive and interactive user interface.

